 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518615,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How much must be deposited annually in a mutual fund that is expected to bear 12.5% interest compounded annually if the account is to be worth $750,000 after 25 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To compute the payment to reach a final goal for an annuity or mutual fund, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{FV \\times \\frac{r}{n}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Round up!</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 1 \\right)\\left( {25} \\right) = 25\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{\\left( {750,000 \\times \\frac{{0.125}}{1}} \\right)}}{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.125}}{1}} \\right)}^{25}} - 1} \\right)}} = \\$5,207.59\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n<p>The annual payment must be $5,207.59.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$5,207.59"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
